renders what it rendered last time:
  1: |
    raw: |
      Redis can be accessed via port 6379   and Sentinel can be accessed via port 26379    on the following DNS name from within your cluster:
      redis.NAMESPACE.svc.cluster.local

      To connect to your Redis server:
      1. To retrieve the redis password:
         echo $(kubectl get secret redis -o "jsonpath={.data['auth']}" | base64 --decode)

      2. Connect to the Redis master pod that you can use as a client. By default the redis-server-0 pod is configured as the master:

         kubectl exec -it redis-server-0 -n NAMESPACE -c redis -- sh

      3. Connect using the Redis CLI (inside container):

         redis-cli -a <REDIS-PASS-FROM-SECRET>
  2: |
    apiVersion: v1
    kind: Service
    metadata:
      annotations: null
      labels:
        app: redis
        chart: redis-4.39.0
        heritage: Helm
        release: instance
      name: redis-announce-0
      namespace: NAMESPACE
    spec:
      ports:
        - name: tcp-server
          port: 6379
          protocol: TCP
          targetPort: redis
        - name: tcp-sentinel
          port: 26379
          protocol: TCP
          targetPort: sentinel
        - name: http-exporter
          port: 9121
          protocol: TCP
          targetPort: exporter-port
      publishNotReadyAddresses: true
